  body: "# Evidence assessment in DMG decisions\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe DMG describes considering evidence,
    establishing facts from it and applying law to those facts, supported by careful recording of conversations
    and interviews.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis is a research model of the captured approach, not an evidential
    scoring algorithm. Direct, indirect and hearsay evidence are distinguished from documentary, oral and real forms;
    admissibility and weight are not the same question.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 01301, PDF page
    41](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=41) — DMG
    Vol 1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n- [DMG 01302, PDF page 41](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=41)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n- [DMG 01310, PDF page 42](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=42)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n- [DMG 01311, PDF page 42](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=42)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n- [DMG 01313, PDF page 42](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=42)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch1` PDF SHA-256: `58b168c7b0a01f54713f6cfa60953549ebc099cbe568ffaeea551d0b756495d2`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `cf7a000e2c54c5361a03ec4ad73fa22cc14e8cdb0d4f03b53919a4a509a6eacb`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
